Thanks for reporting this @jrgleason!

This issue affects Llama 4 (and other models) on AWS Bedrock that require cross-region inference profiles. While OpenCode auto-prefixes Claude and Nova models, Llama 4 currently requires manual configuration.

## Workaround

Specify the prefixed model ID in your `opencode.json`:

```json
{
  "provider": {
    "amazon-bedrock": {
      "models": {
        "us.meta.llama4-maverick-17b-instruct-v1:0": {
          "name": "Llama 4 Maverick"
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "region": "us-east-2"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

See #2746 for more detailed examples of configuring Bedrock inference profiles.

Closing as the workaround is available. If you run into further issues, feel free to reopen!

This issue appears to be resolved in current versions.

**What was fixed:**
1. **Workspace symbol lookup disabled** - The LSP workspace symbol lookup that was causing slowness (particularly with pyright) has been disabled. The `@` file search now uses only the fast fuzzysort-based file index.

2. **Memory leak fixes** - Several memory leak fixes have been merged since this issue was reported, addressing the progressive slowdown when using `/new` within a session.

**If you're still experiencing slowness**, you can disable specific LSP servers via `opencode.json`:

```json
{
  "lsp": {
    "pyright": {
      "disabled": true
    }
  }
}
```

If anyone is still experiencing file search slowness on recent versions (v1.1.x), please open a new issue with repro steps. Thanks!
